            "desc": "5.1 Results\n\n\nTable 1 pools success rate across models and seeds; Table 2\nbreaks it out by model; Table 3 is the Bedrock Sonnet spot check.\n\n\nTable 1: Success rate by optimizer, pooled across models/seeds (bootstrap 95% CI), main matrix.\n\n\n\nDomain\nRandom\nDSPy-static\nBandit\nREINFORCE\n\n\n\n\nTool-use\n0.62 [0.56, 0.69]\n\n0.86 [0.66, 0.98]\n0.61 [0.58, 0.65]\n0.64 [0.59, 0.67]\n\n\nCoding\n0.87 [0.74, 0.97]\n0.88 [0.85, 0.91]\n0.88 [0.77, 0.97]\n\n0.90 [0.80, 0.97]\n\n\nRetrieval QA\n0.20 [0.14, 0.26]\n\n0.31 [0.16, 0.42]\n0.19 [0.09, 0.27]\n0.18 [0.09, 0.23]\n\n\n\n\n\nTable 2: Success rate and avg. tokens/episode by domain ×\\times model ×\\times optimizer.\n\n\n\nDomain\nModel\nRandom\nDSPy-static\nBandit\nREINFORCE\n\n\n\n\nTool-use\nOllama qwen2.5:7b\n0.56 / 480\n0.56 / 286\n0.64 / 509\n0.68 / 528\n\n\nTool-use\nBedrock Haiku\n0.64 / 775\n\n0.96 / 285\n\n0.60 / 616\n0.62 / 680\n\n\nCoding\nOllama qwen2.5:7b\n0.68 / 692\n\n0.88 / 558\n\n0.72 / 676\n0.76 / 653\n\n\nCoding\nBedrock Haiku\n0.94 / 1024\n0.88 / 719\n0.93 / 903\n\n0.95 / 890\n\n\n\nRetrieval QA\nOllama qwen2.5:7b\n0.12 / 678\n0.08 / 266\n0.04 / 764\n0.04 / 591\n\n\nRetrieval QA\nBedrock Haiku\n0.22 / 1188\n\n0.39 / 283\n\n0.24 / 876\n0.23 / 966\n\n\n\n\n\nTable 3: Spot check: Bedrock Sonnet (stronger model), 2 seeds ×\\times 40 episodes.\n\n\n\nDomain\nRandom\nDSPy-static\nBandit\nREINFORCE\n\n\n\n\nTool-use\n0.58\n0.91\n0.60\n0.48\n\n\nCoding\n0.95\n1.00\n0.96\n0.96\n\n\nRetrieval QA\n0.34\n0.53\n0.30\n0.30\n\n\n\n\n\nFigure 1: Reliability vs. cost (avg. tokens per episode) by optimizer, main matrix.\n\n\nThe headline result is not the one we expected. Across every domain and every\nmodel we tested – including the stronger Bedrock Sonnet spot check – the DSPy-optimized\nstatic baseline matches or beats the online, adaptive bandit and REINFORCE\ncontrollers, usually at substantially lower token cost (e.g. tool-use on Bedrock Haiku:\nDSPy-static 96% success at 285 tokens/episode vs. REINFORCE 62% at 680). We report this\ndirectly rather than reframing it, and investigate why in\nSection 5.2.",
